IMPORTANT RULES:
- Generate ONLY questions that can be answered from the provided material
- Do NOT invent facts not present in the material
- Ensure difficulty labels match exactly one of: recall, understanding, application, analysis, evaluation
- Ensure type labels match exactly one of: single_choice, multiple_choice, true_false, matching, ordering, negative_qcm
- For single_choice and multiple_choice: options array is required, correctAnswers must be exact strings from options
- For true_false: set trueFalseAnswer to true or false (boolean)
- For matching: provide matchingPairs as [{left, right}] array
- For ordering: provide orderedItems as a list in correct order
- Every question must have an explanation field
- Return ONLY valid JSON, no markdown, no commentary

Return this exact JSON structure:
{
  "examTitle": "string",
  "questions": [
    {
      "type": "single_choice | multiple_choice | true_false | matching | ordering | negative_qcm",
      "difficulty": "recall | understanding | application | analysis | evaluation",
      "question": "string",
      "options": ["string"],
      "correctAnswers": ["string"],
      "trueFalseAnswer": true,
      "matchingPairs": [{"left": "string", "right": "string"}],
      "orderedItems": ["string"],
      "explanation": "string"
    }
  ]
}
